description:
Show a file to the USER by opening it in an editor window. Input: a file path. Output: only whether the window opened.

This function does NOT read the file: none of its content comes back to you, so calling it teaches you nothing about what is inside. Use it only when the user asked to SEE a file.

To find out what is inside a file, do not call this one:
- a text file (.md, .txt, .csv, .json, .log) -> read it with run_script (cat on macOS/Linux, Get-Content on Windows);
- a document (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx, .pdf) -> open it with the document tools, which return its text, cells or form fields.

Return value:
{
"role": "tool", // Required constant field
"status": "success" | "error",
"error_message": "string | null" // Error details if status = 'error'
}

Example function call parameter: { "path": "/home/user/document.txt" }

Example successful response:
{
"role": "tool",
"status": "success",
"error_message": null
}

Example error response:
{
"role": "tool",
"status": "error",
"error_message": "File not found."
}
